WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.733
Why does a breaker piston get scored?

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:08.133
Dust, metal particles or water in the oil score the surfaces like sandpaper.

3
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:14.900
Clean and cap the hose ends while the breaker is off the machine, and flush new lines before the first run.

4
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:22.167
A worn or wrong-fit bushing holds the tool at an angle; the piston is pushed sideways in the cylinder and scores on one side.

5
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:29.767
When the tool strikes without resting on a surface, the piston runs past its normal stroke towards the front of the cylinder.

6
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:35.833
Thinned oil cannot keep the oil film between piston and cylinder, and metal rubs on metal.
